    abc: "X:1\nT:Young Andrew's Gallop\nO:England\nM:5/4\nC:Andy Hornby\nA:Lancaster\nK:G\nd2 cB A2 G3D| GAB2 G2 A4|\\nd2 cBA2 G3D|1 GAB2 A2 G4 :|2 GAB2 A2 G3:|\nM:7/4\n|:D|\\nGA B2A2 GAB2 A3D| GAB2 A2 GA F2G3D|\\nGAB2 A2 GAB2 A4|\\nM:5/4\nd2 cB A2G3D| GAB2 A2G3 :|\nW:Copyright (C) Andy Hornby July 1997\nM:C|\nThese tunes were originally published in various issues of the\nIrish Pipers' Club newsletter, Iris na bPiobairi, the Pipers' Review.\nThey were published in the hope of providing a few common tunes for\nuilleann pipers, so it seems appropriate to reprint them here to give\nthem a wider exposure.\nJohn Walsh\nwalsh@math.ubca.ca\nFrom the article in the Review:\nThe manuscript tunes given here are lesson pieces played in\nSeattle. Many people from around the country have asked for the\ninclusion of some tunes in the Review in order that a common\nrepertoire can be established. We know well how different regions have\ndissimilar bodies of tunes. This is the first step.\nThe [first] two polkas were collected in Newmarket, Co. Cork in\n1975 from the playing of local musicians. The reel  (The Half-horned Cow) is after the playing of Liam Walsh, a\nWaterford piper (see IPC tape #3). The Lodge Road is a set dance tune\nafter the playing of Sean Maguire, combined with some of the features of\nthe air in O'Neill's 1001 Gems. Miss Monaghan and the Irish Rover are\nafter the piping of Leo Rowsome. The double jig When the Cock Crows...\nis rather faithful to Seamus Ennis' version, and the Mist on the\nValley is largely from the flute-playing of Charley Higgins, Drumkeerin,\nCo. Leitrim.\nJohnny Mickie's Slide is from the playing of Denis Brooks and is\ncopied from a manuscript of his. It also goes well when transposed in G.\nDenis learned it while living in northwest Cork.\nThe final three polkas are from Denis Brooks, who associates them\nwith a great session that took place at the Top of Croom in West Cork whith\nPeter Heelan, Sabra Daly and Seamus Creagh in 1988. They make a nice set.\n--------------------------cut here---------------------------------------\nYou may need the following macros.  Add them to zmacros.tex if they are not\nalready there.\n\def\Zubbzbb#1#2#3#4#5{\Ibu0{#1}{#5}3\qh0{#1}\qh0{#2}\enotes\n\grace\Zlz#3\egrace\notes\qh0{#4}\tqh0{#5}}\n\def\Zlbbzbb#1#2#3#4#5{\Ibl0{#1}{#5}3\qb0{#1}\qb0{#2}\enotes\n\grace\hskip -.5\noteskip\Zuz#3\egrace\notes\qb0{#4}\tqb0{#5}}\n\def\Zlbzbb#1#2#3#4{\Ibl0{#1}{#4}2\qb0{#1}\enotes\n\grace\hskip -.5\noteskip\Zuz#2\egrace\notes\qb0{#3}\tqb0{#4}}\n\def\Zubzbb#1#2#3#4{\Ibu0{#1}{#4}2\qh0{#1}\enotes\n\grace\Zlz#2\egrace\notes\qh0{#3}\tqh0{#4}}\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------\nM:C|"
